Lemma 13: f(f(f(X, W), f(Z, X)), f(W, Z)) = f(f(f(X, Y), f(Z, X)), f(Y, Z)).
Proof:
  f(f(f(X, W), f(Z, X)), f(W, Z))
= { by lemma 2 R->L }
